        "type": "CAMP_LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "in"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "My father knew Ukrainian and he had also studied German in school, so he became a translator for the colonel, and my mother was a cleaning woman for the offices because she was considered trustworthy with her husband working as a translator.",
      "relationship_type": "worked_as",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "My father",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "translator",
        "type": "OCCUPATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "became a"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "One night, when the colonel was away, the SS-officers gathered all the Jews and took them to a place, where a common grave had already been dug.",
      "relationship_type": "taken_to",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "all the Jews",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "common grave",
        "type": "LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "took to"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "They started selecting us - the old and the very young were to be shot, and the young and strong were to be sent to work.",
      "relationship_type": "selected_for",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "the old and the very young",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "shot",
        "type": "ACTION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "to be shot"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "I was sent to the children's row, to the ones to be shot, and my sister was sent to the other.",
      "relationship_type": "selected_for",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "I",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "shot",
        "type": "ACTION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "to be shot"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "On the way back, we heard tractors, but only later we understood why, somebody told us: those tractors, usually used to plough, were let to run in order to cover the noise of the shots and to hide the mass grave.",
      "relationship_type": "killed_in",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "Jews",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "mass grave",
        "type": "LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "shots"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "In the whole ghetto, the only Jews left were us.",
      "relationship_type": "survived",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "us",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "ghetto",
        "type": "GHETTO_LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "left"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "The colonel took us to live in a house, and after three days he came and talked to my mother and father.",
