      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "Shargorod",
        "type": "GHETTO_LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "in"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "We were on the Romanian side, in the spring of 1944 - it was April, I think - when a Russian armored car with the red star on it appeared, and a big fat Russian woman looked out through the cock-pit and shouted, 'Comrades, liberation!'.",
      "relationship_type": "liberated_from",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "We",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "ghetto",
        "type": "GHETTO_LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "liberation"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "I left the ghetto with a cousin of mine, to gather firewood, somewhere near some bombed houses, and some Romanian soldiers caught us and beat us both.",
      "relationship_type": "escaped_from",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "I",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "ghetto",
        "type": "GHETTO_LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "left"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "The Ukrainian woman who had helped me, Irina, came to the gates of the ghetto and told us to stay still because the Soviet army was drawing near; it was just a few kilometers away.",
      "relationship_type": "visited",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "Irina",
        "type": "PERSON"
      },
      "object": {
        "entity": "ghetto",
        "type": "GHETTO_LOCATION"
      },
      "verb_pattern": "came to"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "The first to arrive were the Cossacks on horseback; lots of them.",
